\nB  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nG  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nD  |---------|---------|---------|---------|------5--|---5--7--|7--5-----|5--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nA  |---------|------5--|---5--7--|5--7--8--|7--8-----|8--------|------8--|---8--7--|8--7--5--|7--5-----|5--------|---------|\nE  |5--7--8--|7--8-----|8--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------8--|---8--7--|8--7--5--|\nFinish on the low root; release pressure; move the entire frame one fret.\nContinuous alternate picking - D-start and U-start\n02  BB NATURAL MINOR\nROOT E6  |  FRAME 6-9\n36-NOTE / 12-TRIPLET CELL\nScale tones: Bb C Db Eb F Gb Ab Bb\nDeg|1--2--b3-|2--b3-4--|b3-4--5--|4--5--b6-|5--b6-b7-|b6-b7-8--|8--b7-b6-|b7-b6-5--|b6-5--4--|5--4--b3-|4--b3-2--|b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|\ne  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nB  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nG  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nD  |---------|---------|---------|---------|------6--|---6--8--|8--6-----|6--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nA  |---------|------6--|---6--8--|6--8--9--|8--9-----|9--------|------9--|---9--8--|9--8--6--|8--6-----|6--------|---------|\nE  |6--8--9--|8--9-----|9--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------9--|---9--8--|9--8--6--|\nFinish on the low root; release pressure; move the entire frame one fret.\nContinuous alternate picking - D-start and U-start\n03  B NATURAL MINOR\nROOT E7  |  FRAME 7-10\n36-NOTE / 12-TRIPLET CELL\nScale tones: B C# D E F# G A B\nDeg|1--2--b3-|2--b3-4--|b3-4--5--|4--5--b6-|5--b6-b7-|b6-b7-8--|8--b7-b6-|b7-b6-5--|b6-5--4--|5--4--b3-|4--b3-2--|b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|\ne  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nB  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nG  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nD  |---------|---------|---------|---------|------7--|---7--9--|9--7-----|7--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nA  |---------|------7--|---7--9--|7--9--10-|9--10----|10-------|------10-|---10-9--|10-9--7--|9--7-----|7--------|---------|\nE  |7--9--10-|9--10----|10-------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------10-|---10-9--|10-9--7--|\nFinish on the low root; release pressure; move the entire frame one fret.\nContinuous alternate picking - D-start and U-start\nEighth-note triplets: one three-note group per beat. Keep early and late crossings inside the same pulse.\nPage 3 of 7","text_sha256":"af61ab67099219c4e8b6aae6d92a597757c5f8540d8642c0d82a6000d01d250f"},"L23-PDF-GUIDANCE-P1":{"format":"pdf","page":1,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/PDF version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_23_Natural_Minor_Three_Note_Rolling_Sequence_One_Octave_Neck_Ladder.pdf","sha256":"5601a14c406f3b33e455e96d4539ade22160ed0ac95aa782b36a2ef9d960dd43","text":"Scale Exercises - Section III, Level 23\nNatural Minor Three-Note Rolling Sequence: One-Octave Neck Ladder\nThree notes forward, one degree back.\nLearn the overlap pattern in one octave before extending it across the full six-string frame.\n1. Overlap the minor scale\nPlay 1-2-b3, then begin the next group on degree 2.\nThe line moves forward while revisiting the previous\ntwo notes.\n2. Preserve the pick cycle\nEach triplet has three notes, so its starting stroke\nalternates. Continue through group and string\nboundaries without a reset.\n3. Shift only after the cell\nComplete all 12 triplets, return to the low root, release\npressure, and move the complete frame exactly one\nfret.\nWorked example - A natural minor at low-E fret 5\nScale notes: A B C D E F G A. The octave root is repeated at the turn.\nUP\n1-2-b3 | 2-b3-4 | b3-4-5 | 4-5-b6 | 5-b6-b7 | b6-b7-8\nDOWN\n8-b7-b6 | b7-b6-5 | b6-5-4 | 5-4-b3 | 4-b3-2 | b3-2-1\nDeg|1--2--b3-|2--b3-4--|b3-4--5--|4--5--b6-|5--b6-b7-|b6-b7-8--|8--b7-b6-|b7-b6-5--|b6-5--4--|5--4--b3-|4--b3-2--|b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|\ne  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nB  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nG  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nD  |---------|---------|---------|---------|------5--|---5--7--|7--5-----|5--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nA  |---------|------5--|---5--7--|5--7--8--|7--8-----|8--------|------8--|---8--7--|8--7--5--|7--5-----|5--------|---------|\nE  |5--7--8--|7--8-----|8--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------8--|---8--7--|8--7--5--|\nCROSSINGS\nUP: EEE | EEA | EAA | AAA | AAD | ADD     DOWN: DDA | DAA | AAA | AAE | AEE | EEE\nKEY ROUTE\nA -> Bb -> B -> C -> C# -> D -> Eb -> E -> F -> F# -> G -> G# -> A, then reverse.\nWHY ONE OCTAVE\nLevel 23 isolates the new rolling motion; Level 24 will expand it across six strings.\nSession protocol\n1\nSay the natural-minor formula and\nidentify b3, b6, and b7.\n2\nMaster the A-minor 36-note cell\nbefore adding a shift.\n3\nStart 12-18 BPM below your clean\nLevel 22 tempo.\n4\nUse 2-3 neighboring rungs and\npause one beat after each cell.\n5\nRepeat with a downstroke start\nand an upstroke start.\n6\nRemove the pause, connect the\nroute, and reverse at fret 17.\nSection III now sequences the compact natural-minor shape while preserving the one-fret neck ladder.\nPage 1 of 7","text_sha256":"75baa454e8cd44950db727a6b29ebb1911b75bf4b1259bb4219139a7311599fb"},"L23-TXT-RULE-1-60":{"first_line":1,"format":"txt","last_line":60,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_23_Natural_Minor_Three_Note_Rolling_Sequence_One_Octave_Neck_Ladder.txt","sha256":"c8c01c4a4ad95e1aed5323d485b359a1bd4d057f46fd2b3ffe8277324b0032f7","text":"SCALE EXERCISES - SECTION III, LEVEL 23\nNATURAL MINOR THREE-NOTE ROLLING SEQUENCE - ONE-OCTAVE NECK LADDER: A TO A\n\nPURPOSE\nTurn the straight one-octave natural-minor scale into overlapping three-note groups. Complete the full\n36-note up/down rolling cell, release pressure, move the entire hand-and-thumb frame exactly one fret,\nand repeat through every natural-minor key. Begin with A natural minor at low-E fret 5, climb to A natural\nminor at fret 17, then reverse and return one fret at a time.\n\nWHY THIS LEVEL RETURNS TO ONE OCTAVE\nLevel 22 expanded the straight natural-minor scale across two octaves and all six strings. Level 23\ndeliberately returns to the compact three-string octave so the new overlap pattern can be learned without\nalso managing the upper-octave backreach and B-string offset. Level 24 will extend the sequence later.\n\nIMPORTANT INTERPRETATION\nMoving one fixed scale shape by one fret transposes it. A natural minor is the starting rung, not the key of every rung.\nA fixed-key A-natural-minor exercise in every neck position requires changing the note layout and remains a separate branch.\n\nNATURAL-MINOR FORMULA\nDegrees:   1 2 b3 4 5 b6 b7 8\nIntervals: whole - half - whole - whole - half - whole - whole\n\nCOMPACT ONE-OCTAVE SHAPE - ROOT FRET R ON LOW E\nLow E string: R, R+2, R+3          Fingers 1,3,4\nA string:     R, R+2, R+3          Fingers 1,3,4\nD string:     R, R+2               Fingers 1,3\nThe four-fret hand frame runs from R through R+3.\nAscending notes per string: 3-3-2. Descending notes per string: 2-3-3.\n\nROLLING THREE-NOTE SEQUENCE\nUP:   1-2-b3 | 2-b3-4 | b3-4-5 | 4-5-b6 | 5-b6-b7 | b6-b7-8\nDOWN: 8-b7-b6 | b7-b6-5 | b6-5-4 | 5-4-b3 | 4-b3-2 | b3-2-1\nEach new triplet starts one scale degree farther along. Between groups, the line rolls back one degree.\nDo not pause or reset at a triplet boundary, even when the string crossing moves from late to early.\n\nSTRING-CROSSING MAP\nUP:   EEE | EEA | EAA | AAA | AAD | ADD\nDOWN: DDA | DAA | AAA | AAE | AEE | EEE\nThe all-one-string groups alternate with late and early crossings. Keep the landing note equal in volume.\n\nCELL AND PICKING RULE\nThe complete up/down cell contains 12 triplets and 36 notes. The octave root is repeated at the turn:\nthe last note of b6-b7-8 is followed by the first note of 8-b7-b6. Because 36 is even, the next key\nbegins with the same pick orientation.\nD-start groups: D-U-D | U-D-U | D-U-D | U-D-U ...\nU-start groups: U-D-U | D-U-D | U-D-U | D-U-D ...\nDo not restart the pick cycle at a new triplet, string crossing, scale turn, or one-fret relocation.\n\nNECK ROUTE\nUP:   A(5) > Bb(6) > B(7) > C(8) > C#(9) > D(10) > Eb(11) > E(12) > F(13) > F#(14) > G(15) > G#(16) > A(17)\nDOWN: A(17) > G#(16) > G(15) > F#(14) > F(13) > E(12) > Eb(11) > D(10) > C#(9) > C(8) > B(7) > Bb(6) > A(5)\n\nPRACTICE RULE\nUse eighth-note triplets: one three-note group per beat. Begin 12-18 BPM below your clean Level 22 tempo.\nMaster the A-natural-minor cell alone, then use 2-3 neighboring rungs and pause one beat after each 36-note cell.\nDuring the pause, release pressure and move the complete frame one fret. Repeat with both pick starts.\nThen remove the pause, connect the ladder, reverse at fret 17, and return to fret 5.\nAdd 2 BPM after three clean round trips. Reduce 4-6 BPM after two errors, broken triplet pulse, dragged shift\nnoise, or rising tension. Advance after the complete route is clean with both pick starts on two separate days.\n","text_sha256":"4182503fe57e92ed310992a5fdd3aa468e80589414485b0138fdebead2b9c969"},"L23-TXT-RUNG01-62-73":{"first_line":62,"format":"txt","last_line":73,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/Scale_Exercises_Section_III_Level_23_Natural_Minor_Three_Note_Rolling_Sequence_One_Octave_Neck_Ladder.txt","sha256":"c8c01c4a4ad95e1aed5323d485b359a1bd4d057f46fd2b3ffe8277324b0032f7","text":"RUNG 01 OF 13 - A NATURAL MINOR - ROOT ON LOW E FRET 5 - FRAME 5-8\nScale tones: A B C D E F G A\n36-note cell: six ascending rolling triplets, repeat the octave root at the turn, then six descending triplets.\nDeg|1--2--b3-|2--b3-4--|b3-4--5--|4--5--b6-|5--b6-b7-|b6-b7-8--|8--b7-b6-|b7-b6-5--|b6-5--4--|5--4--b3-|4--b3-2--|b3-2--1--|\nFng|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|\ne  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nB  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nG  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nD  |---------|---------|---------|---------|------5--|---5--7--|7--5-----|5--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nA  |---------|------5--|---5--7--|5--7--8--|7--8-----|8--------|------8--|---8--7--|8--7--5--|7--5-----|5--------|---------|\nE  |5--7--8--|7--8-----|8--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------8--|---8--7--|8--7--5--|\nFinish on the low root, release pressure, and move the entire frame one fret in the route direction.","text_sha256":"11eade5193aafaf5ac9c3e45ccf4ec4e9356a255844930b9b002e6474db40d2c"}}}
